WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.494
With no network, Telo Ride says why live races and group classes are closed, the

00:00:07.494 --> 00:00:08.900
moment it happens.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.533
On Race Setup, Riders online closes and says you're offline; Bots, the default, is

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:17.104
chosen in its place.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.426
On Class Start, Ride with a group closes with its reason, and Ride alone is chosen,

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:29.665
ready to start.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.233
Offline, neither screen asks the service anything. Back online, both ask again at

00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:43.233
once, and the choice opens.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.400
Offline, unreachable or open: one small rule decides, and the screen says which, in

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.088
words.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:05.184
Race Setup offline, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.470
What the tests prove: the reason shows at once, the choice falls back, and it all

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.854
opens again online.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
